Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Metric:", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988667837811783*^9, 
  3.988667838986958*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4df4b0ba-b946-4d41-bbb3-\
f035512ae0d0"],

Cell["\<\
Loss metric is non-infinite lifetime for nontrivial solutions. The best \
lifetime in general is to have a persistent solution and a slow moving glider \
which are separated enough to live for a long time before colliding. This \
gives fairly trivial long-living creatures like such:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988667648237307*^9, 
  3.988667730284107*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f9b58c5c-e31e-45af-a568-\
43a093ee60a4"],

