Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conclusions:", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9886679041077414`*^9, 
  3.9886679056145287`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"69b1167a-272b-4fc2-bb54-\
5318afe3a775"],

Cell["\<\
From what I\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve seen, the genetic algorithm seems to often \
get stuck in local minima. I\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve tried differentiation \
techniques like the GatherBy step in the genetic algorithm, but it doesn\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t seem to help much. This doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t seem \
like a promising approach for finding persistent solutions rather than just \
long-living solutions. When allowing for infinite-lifespan solutions, the \
algorithm seems to converge only on very small infinite solutions, which can \
be just as easily found by random search. This is in contrast to the \
sometimes 60-bit wide persistent solutions that have been found.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988667907500079*^9, 
  3.988668184564334*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b7c6d44e-a9eb-4586-9f94-\
0cee5ca2eda1"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Method 2: Gradient Descent", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988668265854417*^9, 
  3.98866828307364*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"14e89643-fc51-4cee-90b9-\
7e5e90655fe9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Code20 Continuous", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988668628906981*^9, 
  3.9886686335032387`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0afbfdc3-d066-472f-87e5-\
941255996b69"],

Cell["\<\
If code20 could be represented as  a continuous function, then it can undergo \
gradient descent for the largest final solution. This can be found by \
interpolating through the code20 rule to get a continuous function.

One easy way to do it is to simply interpolate some few logic gates, and \
construct code20 from there:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988668285963174*^9, 3.988668370350223*^9}, {
  3.988668531901024*^9, 
  3.988668538729974*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"91938881-248b-4fec-baf5-\
53637f7fcf41"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"NOT", "[", "x_", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"1", "-", "x"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"AND", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "y_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "y"}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"OR", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "y_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"NOT", "[", 
   RowBox[{"AND", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"NOT", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"NOT", "[", "y", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 

 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"XOR", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "y_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"AND", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"NOT", "[", 
      RowBox[{"AND", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"OR", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "a", " ", "small", " ", "representation", " ", "of", " ", "code20", " ", 
    "applied", " ", "to", " ", "neighborhood", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
     "a", ",", " ", "b", ",", " ", "c", ",", " ", "d", ",", " ", "e"}], 
     ")"}]}], " ", "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"code20", "=", 
  RowBox[{"XOR", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"XOR", "[", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"XOR", "[", 
       RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"XOR", "[", 
         RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"XOR", "[", 
           RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", "e"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"OR", "[", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"OR", "[", 
       RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"OR", "[", 
         RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"OR", "[", 
           RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", "e"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988668539988168*^9, 3.988668564392747*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[138]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5d2182d0-c2c2-4eec-8149-ab422aa55b3b"],

